    "explanation": "This is a rider-filed no-show dispute over the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee on TRP-00204. Both sides agree on the arithmetic, so the case turns on a single question: does the driver's verified arrival end the matter, or does POL-NS-04 displace it? It displaces it.\n\nDRIVER — your POL-NS-01 case is accepted in full. Limb (a): the trip record carries an 'arrived' event at 12:41:50. Limb (b): the GPS trace puts you inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE geofence from that very second, with 35 qualifying in-geofence fixes. Limb (c): you held position in one unbroken run of 340 seconds against the 300 second LARGE_VENUE minimum, measured from the first qualifying fix as the clause requires. Limb (d): no boarding event, terminated by you with RIDER_UNREACHABLE, a recognised code. Your POL-NS-05 point is also right — the arrival marker was true (nearest approach 94.9 m, inside the 120 m radius and far inside the 300 m leash, and a held position rather than motion at 15 km/h) — and your POL-NS-06 point is right that the dwell was a 40 second surplus, not a shortfall. That is why no false-arrival referral is made.\n\nBut POL-NS-01 makes the fee chargeable only 'where... no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces them', and POL-NS-04 does displace it on this record. Limbs (a), (b) and (c) all hold. (a) The chat log shows the rider sending locating messages at 12:41:05 ('im at the entrance 3 phv pickup point, which car ah?') and at 12:44:40 ('boss? i still cannot see u leh'), both delivered and both read. (b) You neither replied in the chat within 120 seconds nor placed an in-app call at any point before terminating — no driver message appears in the log at all and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty. (c) The rider track holds 105 qualifying fixes, all within a 39.9 m maximum distance of the pin, well inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE presence radius. RIDER — your POL-NS-04 case is accepted, and your two supporting points are accepted as context: RIDER_UNREACHABLE is a label you entered, not a measurement, and the record shows an unanswered rider at the pin rather than an unreachable one; and the pickup pin is labelled 'Entrance 3', matching the message the driver actually read. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) is not engaged, because the driver was inside the arrival radius rather than merely within 400 m of the pin. On this basis the rider is exonerated and the cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 is refunded in full.\n\nDRIVER — your POL-NS-07 claim for 80 percent (SGD 3.20) is rejected. That clause pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied 'and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it'; POL-NS-04 displaces it, so the precondition fails and no compensation is payable. Your anti-farming point is accepted as accurate — no_show_terminations_30d of 3 is below 4 and 3/142 is below 0.08, so the check would not have tripped — but it is moot once the fee falls.\n\nNo escalation. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, and POL-NS-08 is not engaged on any limb: there is no clock skew (the 12:41:50 arrival matches a GPS fix exactly), no trace defect (100% coverage, 10 second cadence, zero gaps, both tracks present), no chat defect (3 messages reconcile with chat_message_count of 3), and no fare defect (the SGD 4.00 line reconciles with the GREATER of the LARGE_VENUE zone fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee, both SGD 4.00). POL-NS-09 is not met: both counterparty-dispute counters are zero, no_show_disputes_30d is zero, no two admissible artifacts contradict each other, and the anti-farming check does not trip. The only impaired artifact is the TRAFFIC_ADVISORY EV-ADVIS-00204-01, which is MISSING at weight 0.0; neither party relies on it to carry a fact, nothing deciding this case turns on it, and it therefore does not move the confidence cap.\n\nThe contested amount is the SGD 4.00 cancellation-fee line only; the SGD 0.50 platform fee is not in dispute and is not refunded. Confidence is 0.95.",
